    {
      "id": 50048,
      "kind": "statement",
      "difficulty": 55,
      "prompt": "E1 = (1, 2), E2 = (2, 4). Target T = (3, 6) has which property?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "text": "It has infinitely many coefficient pairs because E2 = 2E1."
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "text": "It has exactly one coefficient pair because there are two vectors."
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "It is unreachable because the vectors are dependent."
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "Every coefficient pair produces T."
        }
      ],
      "answer": "A",
      "solution": "Both (u, v) = (3, 0) and (1, 1) work; in general u + 2v = 3. Dependence removes uniqueness, not necessarily existence."
    },
